#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/buying-a-train-ticket.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Buying a train ticket is easier when you know which details to provide and "
"which questions to ask. You usually need to explain your destination, "
"travel date, preferred departure time, and whether you need a one-way or "
"return ticket.\n"
"\n"
"You may also need to compare routes, understand transfers, reserve a seat, "
"or ask about discounts.\n"
"\n"
"## Start the Conversation\n"
"\n"
"At a ticket counter, you can begin with:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I’d like to buy a ticket, please.”\n"
"- “Could I get a ticket to Berlin?”\n"
"- “I need to travel to Kraków tomorrow.”\n"
"- “I’d like to know the best way to get to Prague.”\n"
"- “Could you help me find a train to Warsaw?”\n"
"\n"
"The ticket agent may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Where are you travelling to?”\n"
"- “When would you like to leave?”\n"
"- “Is that for today?”\n"
"- “What time would you like to travel?”\n"
"- “Do you need a one-way or return ticket?”\n"
"- “How many passengers are travelling?”\n"
"\n"
"You can answer clearly and directly:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like a one-way ticket to Gdańsk for tomorrow morning.”\n"
"\n"
"## Say When You Want to Travel\n"
"\n"
"Be as specific as possible about your preferred date and time.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like to travel today.”\n"
"- “I need a ticket for tomorrow morning.”\n"
"- “I’d like to leave at around three.”\n"
"- “Is there a train after six?”\n"
"- “What is the earliest train?”\n"
"- “What is the last train tonight?”\n"
"- “I’d prefer to arrive before noon.”\n"
"- “I can travel at any time after five.”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may offer several options:\n"
"\n"
"> “There is a direct train at 9:20 and another at 10:45.”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ll take the 9:20 train.”\n"
"- “Is there anything earlier?”\n"
"- “What time does the second train arrive?”\n"
"- “Which option is faster?”\n"
"- “Could you check a later train?”\n"
"\n"
"## Choose a One-Way or Return Ticket\n"
"\n"
"A **one-way ticket** covers only the journey to your destination.\n"
"\n"
"A **return ticket** covers the journey to your destination and the journey "
"back.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases:\n"
"\n"
"- “A one-way ticket, please.”\n"
"- “I’d like a return ticket.”\n"
"- “I’m coming back on Sunday.”\n"
"- “Can the return journey be on a different day?”\n"
"- “Is an open return available?”\n"
"- “Is it cheaper to buy a return ticket?”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may ask:\n"
"\n"
"> “When would you like to return?”\n"
"\n"
"You can answer:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like to return on Monday evening, preferably after six.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Direct Trains and Transfers\n"
"\n"
"A direct train takes you to your destination without changing trains.\n"
"\n"
"A journey with a transfer requires you to leave one train and board "
"another.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is it a direct train?”\n"
"- “Do I need to change trains?”\n"
"- “How many transfers are there?”\n"
"- “Where do I need to change?”\n"
"- “How much time do I have between trains?”\n"
"- “Is fifteen minutes enough for the connection?”\n"
"- “Will the connecting train wait if the first train is delayed?”\n"
"- “Do I use the same ticket for both trains?”\n"
"\n"
"You may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “You need to change trains in Poznań.”\n"
"- “There is one transfer.”\n"
"- “You have twenty minutes between trains.”\n"
"- “The direct train is slower but more convenient.”\n"
"- “The faster option requires two changes.”\n"
"\n"
"When comparing routes, think about both travel time and convenience.\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Departure and Arrival Times\n"
"\n"
"Train schedules usually include:\n"
"\n"
"- Departure time\n"
"- Arrival time\n"
"- Journey duration\n"
"- Train number\n"
"- Platform number\n"
"- Number of transfers\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “What time does the train leave?”\n"
"- “What time does it arrive?”\n"
"- “How long does the journey take?”\n"
"- “Which platform does it leave from?”\n"
"- “What is the train number?”\n"
"- “How early should I arrive?”\n"
"- “Where can I check for platform changes?”\n"
"\n"
"To confirm what you heard, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you say the train leaves at 8:15?”\n"
"- “So I arrive at 11:40, correct?”\n"
"- “Was that platform four or platform fourteen?”\n"
"- “Could you write the departure time down for me?”\n"
"\n"
"Confirming numbers is especially useful because times and platform numbers "
"can sound similar.\n"
"\n"
"## Compare Ticket Types\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the railway, several types of tickets may be available.\n"
"\n"
"Common options include:\n"
"\n"
"- Standard ticket\n"
"- First-class ticket\n"
"- Second-class ticket\n"
"- Flexible ticket\n"
"- Non-refundable ticket\n"
"- Off-peak ticket\n"
"- Advance ticket\n"
"- Sleeper ticket\n"
"- Discounted ticket\n"
"\n"
"Questions you can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is the cheapest ticket?”\n"
"- “What is the difference between these options?”\n"
"- “Can I change the departure time?”\n"
"- “Is this ticket refundable?”\n"
"- “Can I cancel it?”\n"
"- “Is the ticket valid on any train?”\n"
"- “Do I have to take this specific train?”\n"
"- “Are there any restrictions?”\n"
"\n"
"A cheaper ticket may offer less flexibility.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “This ticket is cheaper, but it is only valid on the 10:30 train and "
"cannot be refunded.”\n"
"\n"
"Before buying, make sure you understand the conditions.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About First and Second Class\n"
"\n"
"Some trains offer different travel classes.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is a second-class ticket?”\n"
"- “What is the price for first class?”\n"
"- “What is included in first class?”\n"
"- “Is there much difference between the two?”\n"
"- “Does first class include a meal?”\n"
"- “Is Wi-Fi available in both classes?”\n"
"\n"
"You can choose by saying:\n"
"\n"
"- “Second class is fine, thank you.”\n"
"- “I’ll take the first-class option.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer the cheaper ticket.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Seat Reservations\n"
"\n"
"Some tickets include an assigned seat, while others allow you to sit in any "
"available seat.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is a seat reservation included?”\n"
"- “Do I need to reserve a seat?”\n"
"- “Can I choose my seat?”\n"
"- “Could I have a window seat?”\n"
"- “Could I have an aisle seat?”\n"
"- “Can we sit together?”\n"
"- “Is there a table seat available?”\n"
"- “Is the train likely to be busy?”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Your seat is in carriage seven.”\n"
"- “You are in seat 42.”\n"
"- “The reservation costs extra.”\n"
"- “You can sit in any unreserved seat.”\n"
"- “There are no seats together on that train.”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"> “Could you check the next train to see whether two seats together are "
"available?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Discounts\n"
"\n"
"You may qualify for a reduced fare based on your age, status, railway card, "
"or group size.\n"
"\n"
"Possible discounts include:\n"
"\n"
"- Student discounts\n"
"- Youth discounts\n"
"- Senior discounts\n"
"- Child tickets\n"
"- Family tickets\n"
"- Group tickets\n"
"- Railway-card discounts\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “Are there any discounts available?”\n"
"- “Is there a student discount?”\n"
"- “Do children need a ticket?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper family ticket?”\n"
"- “Do you offer group discounts?”\n"
"- “Can I use my railway card?”\n"
"- “Do I need to show proof of eligibility?”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may ask to see a student card, identification document, or "
"discount card.\n"
"\n"
"## Travel with Luggage, a Bicycle, or a Pet\n"
"\n"
"Additional rules or tickets may apply when travelling with large luggage, "
"bicycles, or animals.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is luggage included in the ticket?”\n"
"- “Is there a luggage limit?”\n"
"- “Where can I store my suitcase?”\n"
"- “Can I take a bicycle on this train?”\n"
"- “Do I need a bicycle reservation?”\n"
"- “Can I travel with a dog?”\n"
"- “Do I need to buy a ticket for my dog?”\n"
"- “Are pets allowed in every carriage?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also ask about accessibility:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is the train wheelchair accessible?”\n"
"- “Is step-free boarding available?”\n"
"- “Can someone help me board the train?”\n"
"- “Is there space for a wheelchair?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Services on the Train\n"
"\n"
"For longer journeys, you may want to know what is available on board.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there Wi-Fi on the train?”\n"
"- “Are there power sockets?”\n"
"- “Is there a restaurant carriage?”\n"
"- “Can I buy food on board?”\n"
"- “Is there a toilet on the train?”\n"
"- “Is air conditioning available?”\n"
"- “Is this a sleeper train?”\n"
"- “Are beds or private compartments available?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand the Price\n"
"\n"
"Before paying, confirm the total price and what it includes.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is the ticket?”\n"
"- “Is that the total price?”\n"
"- “Does that include the seat reservation?”\n"
"- “Are there any additional fees?”\n"
"- “Is the return journey included?”\n"
"- “Why is this train more expensive?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper departure time?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also compare options:\n"
"\n"
"> “The direct train costs more. How much would I save by taking the train "
"with one transfer?”\n"
"\n"
"## Pay for the Ticket\n"
"\n"
"At the counter, the agent may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How would you like to pay?”\n"
"- “Are you paying by cash or card?”\n"
"- “Would you like a paper or electronic ticket?”\n"
"- “Would you like the receipt?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful answers include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash?”\n"
"- “Could I have a paper ticket, please?”\n"
"- “Can you send the ticket to my email?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt?”\n"
"- “Where can I find the booking reference?”\n"
"\n"
"After receiving the ticket, check:\n"
"\n"
"- Your name, if required\n"
"- The destination\n"
"- The travel date\n"
"- The departure time\n"
"- The train number\n"
"- The carriage and seat\n"
"- The ticket conditions\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Common Problems\n"
"\n"
"### The preferred train is sold out\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there another train available?”\n"
"- “What is the next departure?”\n"
"- “Are there seats in first class?”\n"
"- “Can I travel without a seat reservation?”\n"
"- “Could you check a different route?”\n"
"\n"
"### The ticket is too expensive\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper option?”\n"
"- “Would travelling later be less expensive?”\n"
"- “Is the train with a transfer cheaper?”\n"
"- “Are there any discounted tickets left?”\n"
"- “Could I take a slower train?”\n"
"\n"
"### The connection is too short\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there an option with a longer transfer?”\n"
"- “What happens if I miss the connection?”\n"
"- “Can I use the next train?”\n"
"- “Will my ticket remain valid?”\n"
"\n"
"### Your plans may change\n"
"\n"
"Ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Can I change this ticket later?”\n"
"- “How much does it cost to change it?”\n"
"- “Can I receive a refund?”\n"
"- “What happens if I miss the train?”\n"
"- “Is a flexible ticket available?”\n"
"\n"
"### The train is delayed or cancelled\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Has the train been delayed?”\n"
"- “How long is the delay?”\n"
"- “Has the train been cancelled?”\n"
"- “Can I use this ticket on another train?”\n"
"- “Where can I request a refund?”\n"
"- “Will I miss my connection?”\n"
"- “Can you help me find another route?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Station Announcements\n"
"\n"
"At the station, you may hear announcements such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “The train has been delayed.”\n"
"- “The platform has changed.”\n"
"- “The train is now departing from platform eight.”\n"
"- “The train has been cancelled.”\n"
"- “This train terminates here.”\n"
"- “Please do not board this train.”\n"
"- “The train is ready for boarding.”\n"
"- “Mind the gap between the train and the platform.”\n"
"\n"
"Check the departure board regularly, because platform numbers may change "
"shortly before departure.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Ticket-Buying Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Traveller:** Hello, I’d like a ticket to Kraków for tomorrow morning.  \n"
"> **Agent:** Certainly. Would you like a one-way or return ticket?  \n"
"> **Traveller:** A return ticket, please. I’d like to come back on Sunday "
"evening.  \n"
"> **Agent:** There is a direct train tomorrow at 9:15. It arrives at 11:50. "
" \n"
"> **Traveller:** Is a seat reservation included?  \n"
"> **Agent:** Yes. Would you prefer a window or aisle seat?  \n"
"> **Traveller:** A window seat, please. How much is the ticket?  \n"
"> **Agent:** The total is 160 złoty.  \n"
"> **Traveller:** Is there a cheaper option?  \n"
"> **Agent:** There is another train at 10:05 with one transfer. It costs "
"125 złoty.  \n"
"> **Traveller:** How long is the transfer?  \n"
"> **Agent:** Twenty-five minutes.  \n"
"> **Traveller:** That sounds fine. I’ll take that option.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Ticket-Buying Formula\n"
"\n"
"When buying a ticket, follow this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Destination:** Say where you want to go.\n"
"2. **Date and time:** Explain when you want to travel.\n"
"3. **Ticket type:** Choose one-way or return.\n"
"4. **Route:** Ask whether the journey is direct.\n"
"5. **Conditions:** Confirm the price, flexibility, and seat reservation.\n"
"6. **Final check:** Repeat the departure time and platform information.\n"
"7. **Payment:** Choose how you want to pay.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like a return ticket to Vienna for Friday morning, returning on "
"Sunday evening. I’d prefer a direct train and a window seat.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are buying a train ticket at Central Station. The AI "
"ticket agent will help you compare departures, ticket types, routes, and "
"prices.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Explain your destination and preferred travel time.\n"
"- Choose between a one-way and return ticket.\n"
"- Ask whether the journey is direct.\n"
"- Confirm the departure and arrival times.\n"
"- Ask about the price and ticket conditions.\n"
"- Request a seat preference.\n"
"- Respond to one complication, such as a sold-out train, a transfer, or a "
"higher-than-expected price.\n"
"- Confirm the final journey details before paying.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on getting the information you need and checking that you have "
"understood it correctly. Perfect grammar is less important than choosing "
"the correct journey and ticket."
msgstr ""
"Comprar un billete de tren es más fácil cuando sabes qué detalles "
"proporcionar y qué preguntas hacer. Por lo general, necesitas explicar tu "
"destino, fecha de viaje, hora de salida preferida y si necesitas un billete "
"de ida o ida y vuelta.\n"
"\n"
"También puede ser necesario comparar rutas, entender transbordos, reservar "
"un asiento o preguntar sobre descuentos.\n"
"\n"
"## Inicia la Conversación\n"
"\n"
"En un mostrador de boletos, puedes comenzar con:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hola, me gustaría comprar un boleto, por favor.”\n"
"- “¿Podría obtener un boleto para Berlín?”\n"
"- “Necesito viajar a Cracovia mañana.”\n"
"- “Me gustaría saber la mejor manera de llegar a Praga.”\n"
"- “¿Podría ayudarme a encontrar un tren a Varsovia?”\n"
"\n"
"El agente de boletos puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Hacia dónde viajas?”\n"
"- “¿Cuándo te gustaría salir?”\n"
"- “¿Es para hoy?”\n"
"- “¿A qué hora te gustaría viajar?”\n"
"- “¿Necesitas un boleto de ida o ida y vuelta?”\n"
"- “¿Cuántos pasajeros viajan?”\n"
"\n"
"Puedes responder clara y directamente:\n"
"\n"
"> “Me gustaría un boleto de ida a Gdańsk para mañana por la mañana.”\n"
"\n"
"## Di Cuándo Quieres Viajar\n"
"\n"
"Sé lo más específico posible sobre tu fecha y hora preferida.\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “Me gustaría viajar hoy.”\n"
"- “Necesito un boleto para mañana por la mañana.”\n"
"- “Me gustaría salir alrededor de las tres.”\n"
"- “¿Hay un tren después de las seis?”\n"
"- “¿Cuál es el primer tren?”\n"
"- “¿Cuál es el último tren de esta noche?”\n"
"- “Preferiría llegar antes del mediodía.”\n"
"- “Puedo viajar en cualquier momento después de las cinco.”\n"
"\n"
"El agente puede ofrecer varias opciones:\n"
"\n"
"> “Hay un tren directo a las 9:20 y otro a las 10:45.”\n"
"\n"
"Puedes responder:\n"
"\n"
"- “Tomaré el tren de las 9:20.”\n"
"- “¿Hay algo más temprano?”\n"
"- “¿A qué hora llega el segundo tren?”\n"
"- “¿Qué opción es más rápida?”\n"
"- “¿Podría revisar un tren más tarde?”\n"
"\n"
"## Elige un Boleto de Ida o Ida y Vuelta\n"
"\n"
"Un **boleto de ida** cubre solo el viaje a tu destino.\n"
"\n"
"Un **boleto de ida y vuelta** cubre el viaje a tu destino y el regreso.\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles:\n"
"\n"
"- “Un boleto de ida, por favor.”\n"
"- “Me gustaría un boleto de ida y vuelta.”\n"
"- “Regreso el domingo.”\n"
"- “¿Puede ser el viaje de regreso en un día diferente?”\n"
"- “¿Está disponible la opción de regreso abierto?”\n"
"- “¿Es más barato comprar un boleto de ida y vuelta?”\n"
"\n"
"El agente puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"> “¿Cuándo te gustaría regresar?”\n"
"\n"
"Puedes responder:\n"
"\n"
"> “Me gustaría regresar el lunes por la tarde, preferiblemente después de "
"las seis.”\n"
"\n"
"## Pregunta por Trenes Directos y Transbordos\n"
"\n"
"Un tren directo te lleva a tu destino sin cambiar de trenes.\n"
"\n"
"Un trayecto con transbordo requiere que dejes un tren y subas a otro.\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Es un tren directo?”\n"
"- “¿Necesito cambiar de tren?”\n"
"- “¿Cuántos transbordos hay?”\n"
"- “¿Dónde necesito cambiar?”\n"
"- “¿Cuánto tiempo tengo entre trenes?”\n"
"- “¿Son quince minutos suficientes para la conexión?”\n"
"- “¿Esperará el tren de conexión si el primer tren se retrasa?”\n"
"- “¿Uso el mismo boleto para ambos trenes?”\n"
"\n"
"Podrías escuchar:\n"
"\n"
"- “Necesitas cambiar de tren en Poznań.”\n"
"- “Hay un transbordo.”\n"
"- “Tienes veinte minutos entre trenes.”\n"
"- “El tren directo es más lento pero más conveniente.”\n"
"- “La opción más rápida requiere dos cambios.”\n"
"\n"
"Al comparar rutas, piensa tanto en el tiempo de viaje como en la "
"conveniencia.\n"
"\n"
"## Entiende los Horarios de Salida y Llegada\n"
"\n"
"Los horarios de los trenes usualmente incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- Hora de salida\n"
"- Hora de llegada\n"
"- Duración del viaje\n"
"- Número de tren\n"
"- Número de andén\n"
"- Número de transbordos\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿A qué hora sale el tren?”\n"
"- “¿A qué hora llega?”\n"
"- “¿Cuánto dura el viaje?”\n"
"- “¿De qué andén sale?”\n"
"- “¿Cuál es el número del tren?”\n"
"- “¿Con cuánto tiempo de anticipación debo llegar?”\n"
"- “¿Dónde puedo verificar cambios de andén?”\n"
"\n"
"Para confirmar lo que escuchaste, di:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Dijiste que el tren sale a las 8:15?”\n"
"- “Entonces, llego a las 11:40, ¿correcto?”\n"
"- “¿Era el andén cuatro o el catorce?”\n"
"- “¿Podrías escribir la hora de salida para mí?”\n"
"\n"
"Confirmar números es especialmente útil porque los horarios y números de "
"andén pueden sonar similares.\n"
"\n"
"## Compara Tipos de Boletos\n"
"\n"
"Dependiendo del ferrocarril, pueden estar disponibles varios tipos de "
"boletos.\n"
"\n"
"Las opciones comunes incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- Boleto estándar\n"
"- Boleto de primera clase\n"
"- Boleto de segunda clase\n"
"- Boleto flexible\n"
"- Boleto no reembolsable\n"
"- Boleto fuera de horas pico\n"
"- Boleto por anticipado\n"
"- Boleto para dormir\n"
"- Boleto con descuento\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas que puedes hacer:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Cuál es el boleto más barato?”\n"
"- “¿Cuál es la diferencia entre estas opciones?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo cambiar la hora de salida?”\n"
"- “¿Es este boleto reembolsable?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo cancelarlo?”\n"
"- “¿Es el boleto válido en cualquier tren?”\n"
"- “¿Tengo que tomar este tren específico?”\n"
"- “¿Hay alguna restricción?”\n"
"\n"
"Un boleto más barato puede ofrecer menos flexibilidad.\n"
"\n"
"Por ejemplo:\n"
"\n"
"> “Este boleto es más barato, pero solo es válido en el tren de las 10:30 y "
"no se puede reembolsar.”\n"
"\n"
"Antes de comprar, asegúrate de entender las condiciones.\n"
"\n"
"## Pregunta por Primera y Segunda Clase\n"
"\n"
"Algunos trenes ofrecen diferentes clases de viaje.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Cuánto cuesta un boleto de segunda clase?”\n"
"- “¿Cuál es el precio para primera clase?”\n"
"- “¿Qué se incluye en primera clase?”\n"
"- “¿Hay mucha diferencia entre las dos?”\n"
"- “¿Incluye comida la primera clase?”\n"
"- “¿Hay Wi-Fi disponible en ambas clases?”\n"
"\n"
"Puedes elegir diciendo:\n"
"\n"
"- “La segunda clase está bien, gracias.”\n"
"- “Tomaré la opción de primera clase.”\n"
"- “Preferiría el boleto más barato.”\n"
"\n"
"## Pregunta por Reservas de Asiento\n"
"\n"
"Algunos boletos incluyen un asiento asignado, mientras que otros te "
"permiten sentarte en cualquier asiento disponible.\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Se incluye una reserva de asiento?”\n"
"- “¿Necesito reservar un asiento?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo elegir mi asiento?”\n"
"- “¿Podría tener un asiento junto a la ventana?”\n"
"- “¿Podría tener un asiento de pasillo?”\n"
"- “¿Podemos sentarnos juntos?”\n"
"- “¿Está disponible un asiento con mesa?”\n"
"- “¿Es probable que el tren esté lleno?”\n"
"\n"
"El agente podría decir:\n"
"\n"
"- “Tu asiento está en el vagón siete.”\n"
"- “Estás en el asiento 42.”\n"
"- “La reserva cuesta extra.”\n"
"- “Puedes sentarte en cualquier asiento no reservado.”\n"
"- “No hay asientos juntos en ese tren.”\n"
"\n"
"Puedes responder:\n"
"\n"
"> “¿Podrías revisar el próximo tren para ver si hay dos asientos juntos "
"disponibles?”\n"
"\n"
"## Pregunta por Descuentos\n"
"\n"
"Podrías calificar para una tarifa reducida en función de tu edad, estado, "
"tarjeta de ferrocarril o tamaño del grupo.\n"
"\n"
"Posibles descuentos incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- Descuentos para estudiantes\n"
"- Descuentos para jóvenes\n"
"- Descuentos para personas mayores\n"
"- Boletos para niños\n"
"- Boletos familiares\n"
"- Boletos grupales\n"
"- Descuentos con tarjeta de ferrocarril\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Hay descuentos disponibles?”\n"
"- “¿Hay un descuento para estudiantes?”\n"
"- “¿Los niños necesitan boleto?”\n"
"- “¿Hay un boleto familiar más barato?”\n"
"- “¿Ofrecen descuentos para grupos?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo usar mi tarjeta de ferrocarril?”\n"
"- “¿Necesito mostrar prueba de elegibilidad?”\n"
"\n"
"El agente puede pedir ver una tarjeta de estudiante, documento de identidad "
"o tarjeta de descuento.\n"
"\n"
"## Viajar con Equipaje, una Bicicleta o una Mascota\n"
"\n"
"Pueden aplicarse reglas adicionales o boletos al viajar con equipaje "
"grande, bicicletas o animales.\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Está incluido el equipaje en el boleto?”\n"
"- “¿Hay un límite de equipaje?”\n"
"- “¿Dónde puedo guardar mi maleta?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo llevar una bicicleta en este tren?”\n"
"- “¿Necesito una reserva para la bicicleta?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo viajar con un perro?”\n"
"- “¿Necesito comprar un boleto para mi perro?”\n"
"- “¿Se permiten mascotas en todos los coches?”\n"
"\n"
"También puedes preguntar sobre accesibilidad:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿El tren es accesible para sillas de ruedas?”\n"
"- “¿Hay embarque sin escalones disponible?”\n"
"- “¿Puede alguien ayudarme a subir al tren?”\n"
"- “¿Hay espacio para una silla de ruedas?”\n"
"\n"
"## Pregunta sobre Servicios en el Tren\n"
"\n"
"Para viajes más largos, es posible que quieras saber qué está disponible a "
"bordo.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Hay Wi-Fi en el tren?”\n"
"- “¿Hay tomas de corriente?”\n"
"- “¿Hay un coche restaurante?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo comprar comida a bordo?”\n"
"- “¿Hay baño en el tren?”\n"
"- “¿Hay aire acondicionado disponible?”\n"
"- “¿Es este un tren nocturno?”\n"
"- “¿Hay camas o compartimentos privados disponibles?”\n"
"\n"
"## Entiende el Precio\n"
"\n"
"Antes de pagar, confirma el precio total y lo que incluye.\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Cuánto cuesta el boleto?”\n"
"- “¿Es ese el precio total?”\n"
"- “¿Incluye eso la reserva de asiento?”\n"
"- “¿Hay tarifas adicionales?”\n"
"- “¿Está incluido el viaje de regreso?”\n"
"- “¿Por qué es más caro este tren?”\n"
"- “¿Hay una hora de salida más barata?”\n"
"\n"
"También puedes comparar opciones:\n"
"\n"
"> “El tren directo cuesta más. ¿Cuánto ahorraría tomando el tren con un "
"transbordo?”\n"
"\n"
"## Paga el Boleto\n"
"\n"
"En el mostrador, el agente puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Cómo te gustaría pagar?”\n"
"- “¿Pagas en efectivo o con tarjeta?”\n"
"- “¿Te gustaría un boleto en papel o electrónico?”\n"
"- “¿Quisieras el recibo?”\n"
"\n"
"Respuestas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “Pagaré con tarjeta.”\n"
"- “¿Puedo pagar en efectivo?”\n"
"- “¿Podría tener un boleto en papel, por favor?”\n"
"- “¿Puede enviar el boleto a mi correo electrónico?”\n"
"- “¿Podría tener un recibo?”\n"
"- “¿Dónde puedo encontrar la referencia de la reserva?”\n"
"\n"
"Después de recibir el boleto, verifica:\n"
"\n"
"- Tu nombre, si es necesario\n"
"- El destino\n"
"- La fecha de viaje\n"
"- La hora de salida\n"
"- El número del tren\n"
"- El vagón y asiento\n"
"- Las condiciones del boleto\n"
"\n"
"## Maneja Problemas Comunes\n"
"\n"
"### El tren preferido está agotado\n"
"\n"
"Puedes preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Hay otro tren disponible?”\n"
"- “¿Cuál es la próxima salida?”\n"
"- “¿Hay asientos en primera clase?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo viajar sin reserva de asiento?”\n"
"- “¿Podrías revisar una ruta diferente?”\n"
"\n"
"### El boleto es demasiado caro\n"
"\n"
"Puedes decir:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Hay una opción más barata?”\n"
"- “¿Sería menos costoso viajar más tarde?”\n"
"- “¿Es más barato el tren con un transbordo?”\n"
"- “¿Quedan boletos con descuento?”\n"
"- “¿Podría tomar un tren más lento?”\n"
"\n"
"### La conexión es demasiado corta\n"
"\n"
"Puedes preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Hay una opción con un transbordo más largo?”\n"
"- “¿Qué pasa si pierdo la conexión?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo usar el próximo tren?”\n"
"- “¿Mi boleto seguirá siendo válido?”\n"
"\n"
"### Tus planes pueden cambiar\n"
"\n"
"Pregunta:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Puedo cambiar este boleto más tarde?”\n"
"- “¿Cuánto cuesta cambiarlo?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo recibir un reembolso?”\n"
"- “¿Qué pasa si pierdo el tren?”\n"
"- “¿Está disponible un boleto flexible?”\n"
"\n"
"### El tren está retrasado o cancelado\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- “¿Se ha retrasado el tren?”\n"
"- “¿Cuánto dura el retraso?”\n"
"- “¿Se ha cancelado el tren?”\n"
"- “¿Puedo usar este boleto en otro tren?”\n"
"- “¿Dónde puedo solicitar un reembolso?”\n"
"- “¿Perderé mi conexión?”\n"
"- “¿Puede ayudarme a encontrar otra ruta?”\n"
"\n"
"## Entiende Anuncios en la Estación\n"
"\n"
"En la estación, puedes escuchar anuncios como:\n"
"\n"
"- “El tren se ha retrasado.”\n"
"- “El andén ha cambiado.”\n"
"- “El tren ahora sale del andén ocho.”\n"
"- “El tren ha sido cancelado.”\n"
"- “Este tren termina su recorrido aquí.”\n"
"- “Por favor, no abordes este tren.”\n"
"- “El tren está listo para el embarque.”\n"
"- “Cuidado con el hueco entre el tren y el andén.”\n"
"\n"
"Revisa el tablero de salidas regularmente, ya que los números de andén "
"pueden cambiar poco antes de la salida.\n"
"\n"
"## Una Conversación Sencilla para Comprar Boletos\n"
"\n"
"Una conversación típica puede ser así:\n"
"\n"
"> **Viajero:** Hola, me gustaría un boleto a Cracovia para mañana por la "
"mañana.  \n"
"> **Agente:** Claro. ¿Te gustaría un boleto de ida o ida y vuelta?  \n"
"> **Viajero:** Un boleto de ida y vuelta, por favor. Me gustaría regresar "
"el domingo por la noche.  \n"
"> **Agente:** Hay un tren directo mañana a las 9:15. Llega a las 11:50.  \n"
"> **Viajero:** ¿Está incluida la reserva de asiento?  \n"
"> **Agente:** Sí. ¿Prefieres asiento junto a la ventana o al pasillo?  \n"
"> **Viajero:** Un asiento junto a la ventana, por favor. ¿Cuánto cuesta el "
"boleto?  \n"
"> **Agente:** El total es 160 złoty.  \n"
"> **Viajero:** ¿Hay una opción más barata?  \n"
"> **Agente:** Hay otro tren a las 10:05 con un transbordo. Cuesta 125 "
"złoty.  \n"
"> **Viajero:** ¿Cuánto dura el transbordo?  \n"
"> **Agente:** Veinticinco minutos.  \n"
"> **Viajero:** Eso suena bien. Tomaré esa opción.\n"
"\n"
"## Una Fórmula Sencilla para Comprar Boletos\n"
"\n"
"Al comprar un boleto, sigue esta estructura:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Destino:** Di a dónde quieres ir.\n"
"2. **Fecha y hora:** Explica cuándo quieres viajar.\n"
"3. **Tipo de boleto:** Elige ida o ida y vuelta.\n"
"4. **Ruta:** Pregunta si el trayecto es directo.\n"
"5. **Condiciones:** Confirma el precio, flexibilidad y reserva de asiento.\n"
"6. **Verificación final:** Repite la hora de salida y la información del "
"andén.\n"
"7. **Pago:** Elige cómo deseas pagar.\n"
"\n"
"Por ejemplo:\n"
"\n"
"> “Me gustaría un boleto de ida y vuelta a Viena para el viernes por la "
"mañana, regresando el domingo por la noche. Preferiría un tren directo y un "
"asiento junto a la ventana.”\n"
"\n"
"## Escenario de Práctica\n"
"\n"
"En este juego de roles, estás comprando un boleto de tren en la Estación "
"Central. El agente de boletos de IA te ayudará a comparar salidas, tipos de "
"boletos, rutas y precios.\n"
"\n"
"Durante la conversación, intenta:\n"
"\n"
"- Explicar tu destino y hora de viaje preferida.\n"
"- Elegir entre un boleto de ida y de ida y vuelta.\n"
"- Preguntar si el trayecto es directo.\n"
"- Confirmar las horas de salida y llegada.\n"
"- Preguntar sobre el precio y condiciones del boleto.\n"
"- Solicitar una preferencia de asiento.\n"
"- Responder a una complicación, como un tren agotado, un transbordo o un "
"precio más alto de lo esperado.\n"
"- Confirmar los detalles finales del viaje antes de pagar.\n"
"\n"
"Concéntrate en obtener la información que necesitas y verifica que la hayas "
"entendido correctamente. La gramática perfecta es menos importante que "
"elegir el trayecto y boleto correctos."

