#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/in-the-restaurant.ts:58
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Eating at a restaurant involves several short conversations: asking for a "
"table, understanding the menu, ordering food, making requests, handling "
"problems, and paying the bill.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need complicated sentences. Clear questions, polite requests, "
"and confirming important details will help you communicate successfully.\n"
"\n"
"## Arriving at the Restaurant\n"
"\n"
"When you enter, a member of staff may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have a reservation?”\n"
"- “What name is the reservation under?”\n"
"- “How many people are in your party?”\n"
"- “Would you prefer to sit inside or outside?”\n"
"- “Would you like a table by the window?”\n"
"- “Is this table all right?”\n"
"\n"
"If you have a reservation, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I have a reservation.”\n"
"- “The reservation is under Dmowski.”\n"
"- “I booked a table for two at seven.”\n"
"- “We should have a reservation for four people.”\n"
"- “One more person will be joining us shortly.”\n"
"\n"
"If you do not have a reservation, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have a table for two?”\n"
"- “We don’t have a reservation. Is there anything available?”\n"
"- “How long is the wait for a table?”\n"
"- “Could we sit outside?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to sit somewhere quiet?”\n"
"\n"
"You may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Your table will be ready in about fifteen minutes.”\n"
"- “We only have tables outside at the moment.”\n"
"- “We can seat you at the bar.”\n"
"- “Unfortunately, we are fully booked.”\n"
"- “Please follow me.”\n"
"\n"
"## Asking for the Menu\n"
"\n"
"After you sit down, the waiter may give you a menu and ask about drinks.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we see the menu, please?”\n"
"- “Do you have a menu in English?”\n"
"- “Could I have the drinks menu?”\n"
"- “Do you have a children’s menu?”\n"
"- “Is there a separate dessert menu?”\n"
"- “Could we have a few more minutes?”\n"
"\n"
"If you are not ready to order, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “We’re still deciding.”\n"
"- “Could you give us another minute?”\n"
"- “I’m ready to order drinks, but not food yet.”\n"
"- “Could you come back in five minutes?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to rush. It is normal to ask for more time.\n"
"\n"
"## Ordering Drinks\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Can I get you something to drink?”\n"
"- “Would you like still or sparkling water?”\n"
"- “Can I bring you anything from the bar?”\n"
"- “Would you like to see the wine list?”\n"
"\n"
"You can order by saying:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I have a glass of water, please?”\n"
"- “I’d like a sparkling water.”\n"
"- “Could we have a bottle of still water for the table?”\n"
"- “I’ll have an orange juice.”\n"
"- “Could I get a coffee after the meal?”\n"
"- “What non-alcoholic drinks do you have?”\n"
"- “Do you have any alcohol-free beer?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful water vocabulary:\n"
"\n"
"- **Still water** — water without bubbles\n"
"- **Sparkling water** — carbonated water\n"
"- **Tap water** — water from the public water supply\n"
"- **Bottled water** — water served from a bottle\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is tap water available?”\n"
"- “Is the water complimentary?”\n"
"- “Could we have some ice?”\n"
"- “Could I have that without ice?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understanding the Menu\n"
"\n"
"Menus often contain unfamiliar ingredients or cooking methods. It is "
"completely normal to ask questions.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is this dish?”\n"
"- “What does this come with?”\n"
"- “How is it prepared?”\n"
"- “What kind of meat is used?”\n"
"- “Is this dish spicy?”\n"
"- “Is it very rich?”\n"
"- “Is this served hot or cold?”\n"
"- “What is the sauce made from?”\n"
"- “Does this come with a side dish?”\n"
"- “Is this enough for one person?”\n"
"- “Could you explain the difference between these two dishes?”\n"
"\n"
"Common menu sections include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Starter or appetizer** — a small dish served before the main course\n"
"- **Main course or entrée** — the central dish of the meal\n"
"- **Side dish** — a smaller dish served with the main course\n"
"- **Dessert** — a sweet dish served at the end\n"
"- **Special** — a dish that may only be available that day\n"
"- **Set menu** — several courses offered together for a fixed price\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for a Recommendation\n"
"\n"
"When you are unsure what to order, ask the waiter for help.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “What would you recommend?”\n"
"- “What is your most popular dish?”\n"
"- “What is today’s special?”\n"
"- “Which dish is not too spicy?”\n"
"- “What would you recommend for someone who likes fish?”\n"
"- “I’d like something light. What would you suggest?”\n"
"- “Which vegetarian dish would you recommend?”\n"
"- “What is the difference between these two options?”\n"
"\n"
"It helps to explain your preferences:\n"
"\n"
"- “I like spicy food.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer something light.”\n"
"- “I don’t eat red meat.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for something filling.”\n"
"- “I’d like to try something local.”\n"
"- “I don’t like very sweet sauces.”\n"
"\n"
"A good recommendation should match what you enjoy, not simply what is "
"popular.\n"
"\n"
"## Place Your Order\n"
"\n"
"Common ways to order include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like the tomato soup to start.”\n"
"- “I’ll have the grilled salmon.”\n"
"- “Could I get the chicken salad?”\n"
"- “For my main course, I’d like the pasta.”\n"
"- “I think I’ll try the daily special.”\n"
"- “We’d like to share the starter.”\n"
"- “Could we order one more side dish?”\n"
"\n"
"A typical order might sound like this:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like the mushroom soup as a starter and the grilled chicken for my "
"main course. Could I have the salad instead of the fries?”\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Are you ready to order?”\n"
"- “What would you like to start with?”\n"
"- “And for your main course?”\n"
"- “Would you like any side dishes?”\n"
"- “How would you like your steak cooked?”\n"
"- “Would you like anything else?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for Changes to a Dish\n"
"\n"
"Restaurants can often make small changes, although not every request will "
"be possible.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I have this without onions?”\n"
"- “Could you leave out the cheese?”\n"
"- “Could I have the sauce on the side?”\n"
"- “Can I replace the fries with a salad?”\n"
"- “Could I add some grilled vegetables?”\n"
"- “Could you make it less spicy?”\n"
"- “Could I have the dressing separately?”\n"
"- “Is it possible to order a smaller portion?”\n"
"- “Could we share this dish?”\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Certainly.”\n"
"- “That should be possible.”\n"
"- “There is an additional charge.”\n"
"- “Unfortunately, the sauce is prepared in advance.”\n"
"- “You can choose a different side.”\n"
"- “Let me check with the kitchen.”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain Allergies and Dietary Requirements\n"
"\n"
"Tell the waiter clearly if you have an allergy or an important dietary "
"restriction.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to peanuts.”\n"
"- “I have a severe nut allergy.”\n"
"- “I cannot eat gluten.”\n"
"- “I’m lactose intolerant.”\n"
"- “I don’t eat meat.”\n"
"- “I’m vegan.”\n"
"- “I need a dairy-free option.”\n"
"- “Does this contain shellfish?”\n"
"- “Is this suitable for vegetarians?”\n"
"- “Could you check with the kitchen?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this prepared near any nuts?”\n"
"- “Does the sauce contain dairy?”\n"
"- “Is the soup made with chicken stock?”\n"
"- “Does this contain raw egg?”\n"
"- “Is there a gluten-free version?”\n"
"- “Can this dish be prepared without cheese?”\n"
"\n"
"For a serious allergy, do not rely only on symbols printed on the menu. "
"Explain the allergy directly and ask the waiter to confirm with the "
"kitchen.\n"
"\n"
"## Choose How Meat Is Cooked\n"
"\n"
"When ordering steak or some other meats, the waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"> “How would you like that cooked?”\n"
"\n"
"Common options include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Rare** — cooked briefly and red inside\n"
"- **Medium rare** — warm and red in the centre\n"
"- **Medium** — pink in the centre\n"
"- **Medium well** — only slightly pink\n"
"- **Well done** — fully cooked through\n"
"\n"
"You can answer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Medium, please.”\n"
"- “I’d like it well done.”\n"
"- “Could you cook it medium rare?”\n"
"- “Please make sure it is fully cooked.”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm Your Order\n"
"\n"
"Before leaving the table, the waiter may repeat the order.\n"
"\n"
"Listen carefully and correct any mistakes:\n"
"\n"
"- “Yes, that’s correct.”\n"
"- “Actually, I ordered the salmon, not the chicken.”\n"
"- “The salad should be without onions.”\n"
"- “We ordered two soups, not one.”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the side dishes?”\n"
"- “Does that include the extra vegetables?”\n"
"- “Yes, but please put the sauce on the side.”\n"
"\n"
"Repeating important details helps prevent misunderstandings.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for Something During the Meal\n"
"\n"
"You may need an extra item after the food arrives.\n"
"\n"
"Useful requests include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we have some more water?”\n"
"- “Could I get another fork?”\n"
"- “Could we have some extra napkins?”\n"
"- “Could I have some salt and pepper?”\n"
"- “Could you bring us another plate?”\n"
"- “Could I have some ketchup?”\n"
"- “Could we get another basket of bread?”\n"
"- “Could you warm this up, please?”\n"
"- “Could I order another drink?”\n"
"\n"
"To get the waiter’s attention politely, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me.”\n"
"- “Sorry, could you help us?”\n"
"- “When you have a moment, could we have some more water?”\n"
"\n"
"Avoid shouting or snapping your fingers.\n"
"\n"
"## Respond When the Waiter Checks on You\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How is everything?”\n"
"- “Is your food all right?”\n"
"- “Can I get you anything else?”\n"
"- “Are you enjoying your meal?”\n"
"\n"
"If everything is good, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Everything is great, thank you.”\n"
"- “The food is delicious.”\n"
"- “Yes, everything is fine.”\n"
"- “We’re enjoying it, thank you.”\n"
"\n"
"If something is wrong, this is a good opportunity to explain it.\n"
"\n"
"## Handle an Incorrect Order\n"
"\n"
"Mistakes can happen. Explain the problem calmly and clearly.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, I think this is the wrong dish.”\n"
"- “I ordered the salmon, but this is chicken.”\n"
"- “I asked for this without cheese.”\n"
"- “This isn’t what I ordered.”\n"
"- “We’re still waiting for one dish.”\n"
"- “I think this belongs to another table.”\n"
"- “Could you check our order, please?”\n"
"\n"
"Ask for a clear solution:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you replace it, please?”\n"
"- “Could you bring the dish I ordered?”\n"
"- “Could you remove this from the bill?”\n"
"- “Could you check how long the correct dish will take?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to keep the other meals warm?”\n"
"\n"
"## Complain About the Food Politely\n"
"\n"
"If the food is not properly prepared, describe the specific problem.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “The food is cold.”\n"
"- “The steak is overcooked.”\n"
"- “This is much spicier than I expected.”\n"
"- “The chicken does not seem fully cooked.”\n"
"- “The soup is too salty.”\n"
"- “There is an ingredient I asked to have removed.”\n"
"- “This dish tastes unusual.”\n"
"- “Could you ask the kitchen to check it?”\n"
"\n"
"A polite but clear complaint might be:\n"
"\n"
"> “Excuse me, I ordered the steak medium, but it is well done. Would it be "
"possible to replace it?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to apologize for reporting a genuine problem.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About a Delayed Order\n"
"\n"
"If you have been waiting a long time, ask for an update:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, could you check on our order?”\n"
"- “Do you know how much longer it will take?”\n"
"- “We’ve been waiting for about forty minutes.”\n"
"- “Is there a delay in the kitchen?”\n"
"- “One person at our table still hasn’t received their food.”\n"
"- “Could all the meals be served together?”\n"
"- “We need to leave soon. Is the order almost ready?”\n"
"\n"
"Stay factual and explain what you need.\n"
"\n"
"## Order Dessert or Coffee\n"
"\n"
"After the main course, the waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would you like to see the dessert menu?”\n"
"- “Can I interest you in dessert?”\n"
"- “Would you like coffee or tea?”\n"
"- “Can I clear these plates?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we see the dessert menu?”\n"
"- “What desserts do you recommend?”\n"
"- “We’ll share one dessert.”\n"
"- “I’ll have a coffee, please.”\n"
"- “Could I have a decaffeinated coffee?”\n"
"- “No dessert, thank you.”\n"
"- “Just the bill, please.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask to Take Leftovers Home\n"
"\n"
"In some countries and restaurants, you can ask to take unfinished food with "
"you.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I take this home?”\n"
"- “Could you pack this for me?”\n"
"- “Could I have a takeaway box?”\n"
"- “Could you pack the sauce separately?”\n"
"- “Is it safe to reheat this tomorrow?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would you like me to box that for you?”\n"
"- “Would you like to take the rest with you?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for the Bill\n"
"\n"
"At the end of the meal, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we have the bill, please?”\n"
"- “Could I get the check, please?”\n"
"- “We’re ready to pay.”\n"
"- “Could you bring the card machine?”\n"
"- “Can we pay at the table?”\n"
"- “Do we pay here or at the counter?”\n"
"\n"
"**Bill** is more common in British English, while **check** is more common "
"in American English.\n"
"\n"
"## Pay Together or Separately\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Will that be together or separate?”\n"
"- “Would you like to split the bill?”\n"
"- “How would you like to pay?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful responses include:\n"
"\n"
"- “We’ll pay together.”\n"
"- “Could we pay separately?”\n"
"- “Could we split the bill equally?”\n"
"- “I’ll pay for everything.”\n"
"- “Could I pay for these two items?”\n"
"- “Can we use two different cards?”\n"
"- “Could you divide the total between three people?”\n"
"\n"
"If you need to explain exactly what you ordered, say:\n"
"\n"
"> “I had the soup, the salmon, and one sparkling water.”\n"
"\n"
"## Check the Bill\n"
"\n"
"Before paying, check that the items and total are correct.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you explain this charge?”\n"
"- “I think there is an extra item on the bill.”\n"
"- “We only ordered one bottle of water.”\n"
"- “Was the service charge included?”\n"
"- “Is the tip already included?”\n"
"- “Could you remove this item? It was sent back.”\n"
"- “Could I have an itemized bill?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt?”\n"
"\n"
"An **itemized bill** lists each food and drink item separately.\n"
"\n"
"## Pay and Leave a Tip\n"
"\n"
"Useful payment phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash?”\n"
"- “Do you accept contactless payments?”\n"
"- “Could I pay in a different currency?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt?”\n"
"- “Can I add a tip by card?”\n"
"- “Is service included?”\n"
"- “Please keep the change.”\n"
"\n"
"Tipping customs vary by country. Check whether a service charge has already "
"been added before leaving an additional tip.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Restaurant Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Waiter:** Good evening. Do you have a reservation?  \n"
"> **Customer:** Yes, I booked a table for two under Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Certainly. Please follow me. Can I bring you something to "
"drink?  \n"
"> **Customer:** Could we have a bottle of still water, please?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Of course. Are you ready to order?  \n"
"> **Customer:** I need another minute. What would you recommend for someone "
"who likes fish?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** The grilled salmon is very popular. It comes with potatoes "
"and vegetables.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Does the sauce contain dairy?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Yes, but we can serve it without the sauce.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Great. I’ll have the salmon without the sauce. Could I "
"replace the potatoes with a salad?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Certainly.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Thank you.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Restaurant Formula\n"
"\n"
"Use this structure during a restaurant visit:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Arrive:** Confirm your reservation or ask for a table.\n"
"2. **Ask:** Request the menu and ask about unfamiliar dishes.\n"
"3. **Choose:** Order food and drinks clearly.\n"
"4. **Clarify:** Explain allergies, preferences, and requested changes.\n"
"5. **Confirm:** Listen while the waiter repeats the order.\n"
"6. **Respond:** Ask for anything else you need during the meal.\n"
"7. **Resolve:** Explain any problems and request a solution.\n"
"8. **Pay:** Ask for the bill, check it, and choose a payment method.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like the grilled chicken, but could I have it without onions and "
"with a salad instead of fries?”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are dining at the Riverside Kitchen. The AI waiter "
"will welcome you, help you understand the menu, take your order, and "
"respond to your requests.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask for a table or confirm a reservation.\n"
"- Order a drink and a main course.\n"
"- Ask at least one question about a menu item.\n"
"- Request a recommendation.\n"
"- Mention a dietary preference or ask for a change.\n"
"- Confirm an important detail about your order.\n"
"- Respond to one small problem with the meal or service.\n"
"- Ask for the bill and explain how you would like to pay.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating clearly and politely. Perfect grammar is less "
"important than making sure the waiter understands your order and your needs."
msgstr ""
"Comer en un restaurante implica varias conversaciones cortas: pedir una "
"mesa, entender el menú, pedir comida, hacer solicitudes, manejar problemas "
"y pagar la cuenta.\n"
"\n"
"No necesitas oraciones complicadas. Las preguntas claras, las peticiones "
"amables y la confirmación de detalles importantes te ayudarán a comunicarte "
"con éxito.\n"
"\n"
"## Llegando al Restaurante\n"
"\n"
"Cuando entras, un miembro del personal puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Tiene una reserva?\"\n"
"- \"¿A nombre de quién está la reserva?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cuántas personas hay en su grupo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Prefiere sentarse adentro o afuera?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría una mesa junto a la ventana?\"\n"
"- \"¿Está bien esta mesa?\"\n"
"\n"
"Si tienes una reserva, puedes decir:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hola, tengo una reserva.\"\n"
"- \"La reserva está a nombre de Dmowski.\"\n"
"- \"Reservé una mesa para dos a las siete.\"\n"
"- \"Deberíamos tener una reserva para cuatro personas.\"\n"
"- \"Otra persona se unirá a nosotros en breve.\"\n"
"\n"
"Si no tienes una reserva, di:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Tiene una mesa para dos?\"\n"
"- \"No tenemos una reserva. ¿Hay algo disponible?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cuánto tiempo se espera por una mesa?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos sentarnos afuera?\"\n"
"- \"¿Sería posible sentarse en un lugar tranquilo?\"\n"
"\n"
"Podrías escuchar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Su mesa estará lista en unos quince minutos.\"\n"
"- \"Solo tenemos mesas afuera en este momento.\"\n"
"- \"Podemos acomodarle en el bar.\"\n"
"- \"Desafortunadamente, estamos completamente reservados.\"\n"
"- \"Por favor, sígame.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir el Menú\n"
"\n"
"Después de sentarte, el camarero puede darte un menú y preguntar sobre "
"bebidas.\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos ver el menú, por favor?\"\n"
"- \"¿Tiene un menú en inglés?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener el menú de bebidas?\"\n"
"- \"¿Tiene un menú para niños?\"\n"
"- \"¿Hay un menú de postres separado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos tener unos minutos más?\"\n"
"\n"
"Si no estás listo para ordenar, di:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Todavía estamos decidiendo.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría darnos otro minuto?\"\n"
"- \"Estoy listo para pedir bebidas, pero aún no la comida.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría regresar en cinco minutos?\"\n"
"\n"
"No necesitas apresurarte. Es normal pedir más tiempo.\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir Bebidas\n"
"\n"
"El camarero puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Le traigo algo de beber?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría agua con gas o sin gas?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le traigo algo del bar?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría ver la carta de vinos?\"\n"
"\n"
"Puedes pedir diciendo:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener un vaso de agua, por favor?\"\n"
"- \"Me gustaría un agua con gas.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos tener una botella de agua sin gas para la mesa?\"\n"
"- \"Tomaré un jugo de naranja.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tomar un café después de la comida?\"\n"
"- \"¿Qué bebidas no alcohólicas tienen?\"\n"
"- \"¿Tienen alguna cerveza sin alcohol?\"\n"
"\n"
"Vocabulario útil sobre el agua:\n"
"\n"
"- **Agua sin gas** — agua sin burbujas\n"
"- **Agua con gas** — agua carbonatada\n"
"- **Agua de grifo** — agua del suministro público\n"
"- **Agua embotellada** — agua servida de una botella\n"
"\n"
"Puedes preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Hay agua de grifo disponible?\"\n"
"- \"¿El agua es de cortesía?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos tener un poco de hielo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener eso sin hielo?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Entender el Menú\n"
"\n"
"Los menús a menudo contienen ingredientes o métodos de cocción "
"desconocidos. Es completamente normal hacer preguntas.\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Qué es este plato?\"\n"
"- \"¿Con qué viene esto?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cómo se prepara?\"\n"
"- \"¿Qué tipo de carne se usa?\"\n"
"- \"¿Este plato es picante?\"\n"
"- \"¿Es muy pesado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Se sirve caliente o frío?\"\n"
"- \"¿De qué está hecha la salsa?\"\n"
"- \"¿Esto viene con un acompañamiento?\"\n"
"- \"¿Es suficiente para una persona?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría explicar la diferencia entre estos dos platos?\"\n"
"\n"
"Las secciones comunes de un menú incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- **Entrada o aperitivo** — un plato pequeño servido antes del plato "
"principal\n"
"- **Plato principal** — el plato central de la comida\n"
"- **Acompañamiento** — un plato más pequeño servido con el plato principal\n"
"- **Postre** — un plato dulce servido al final\n"
"- **Especial** — un plato que puede estar disponible solo ese día\n"
"- **Menú del día** — varios platos ofrecidos juntos por un precio fijo\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir una Recomendación\n"
"\n"
"Cuando no estás seguro de qué pedir, pregunta al camarero por ayuda.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes decir:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Qué recomendaría?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cuál es su plato más popular?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cuál es la especialidad de hoy?\"\n"
"- \"¿Qué plato no es muy picante?\"\n"
"- \"¿Qué recomendaría para alguien que le gusta el pescado?\"\n"
"- \"Me gustaría algo ligero. ¿Qué sugeriría?\"\n"
"- \"¿Qué plato vegetariano recomendaría?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cuál es la diferencia entre estas dos opciones?\"\n"
"\n"
"Ayuda explicar tus preferencias:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Me gusta la comida picante.\"\n"
"- \"Preferiría algo ligero.\"\n"
"- \"No como carne roja.\"\n"
"- \"Busco algo que me llene.\"\n"
"- \"Me gustaría probar algo local.\"\n"
"- \"No me gustan las salsas muy dulces.\"\n"
"\n"
"Una buena recomendación debe coincidir con lo que disfrutas, no simplemente "
"con lo que es popular.\n"
"\n"
"## Hacer Tu Pedido\n"
"\n"
"Las formas comunes de pedir incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Me gustaría la sopa de tomate para empezar.\"\n"
"- \"Tomaré el salmón a la parrilla.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener la ensalada de pollo?\"\n"
"- \"Para mi plato principal, me gustaría la pasta.\"\n"
"- \"Creo que probaré el especial del día.\"\n"
"- \"Nos gustaría compartir la entrada.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos pedir otro acompañamiento más?\"\n"
"\n"
"Un pedido típico podría sonar así:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Me gustaría la sopa de champiñones como entrada y el pollo a la "
"parrilla para mi plato principal. ¿Podría tener la ensalada en lugar de las "
"papas fritas?\"\n"
"\n"
"El camarero puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Está listo para pedir?\"\n"
"- \"¿Con qué gustaría empezar?\"\n"
"- \"¿Y para su plato principal?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría algún acompañamiento?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cómo le gustaría que cocináramos el bistec?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría algo más?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir Cambios a un Plato\n"
"\n"
"Los restaurantes a menudo pueden hacer pequeños cambios, aunque no siempre "
"cada solicitud será posible.\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener esto sin cebolla?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría omitir el queso?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener la salsa a un lado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Puedo cambiar las papas fritas por una ensalada?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría agregar verduras a la parrilla?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría hacerlo menos picante?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener el aderezo por separado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Es posible pedir una porción más pequeña?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos compartir este plato?\"\n"
"\n"
"El camarero puede responder:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Por supuesto.\"\n"
"- \"Eso debería ser posible.\"\n"
"- \"Hay un cargo adicional.\"\n"
"- \"Desafortunadamente, la salsa se prepara por adelantado.\"\n"
"- \"Puede elegir un acompañamiento diferente.\"\n"
"- \"Déjeme consultar con la cocina.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Explicar Alergias y Requisitos Dietéticos\n"
"\n"
"Dile al camarero claramente si tienes una alergia o una restricción "
"dietética importante.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes decir:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Soy alérgico a los cacahuetes.\"\n"
"- \"Tengo una alergia severa a las nueces.\"\n"
"- \"No puedo comer gluten.\"\n"
"- \"Soy intolerante a la lactosa.\"\n"
"- \"No como carne.\"\n"
"- \"Soy vegano.\"\n"
"- \"Necesito una opción libre de lácteos.\"\n"
"- \"¿Esto contiene mariscos?\"\n"
"- \"¿Esto es adecuado para vegetarianos?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría consultar con la cocina?\"\n"
"\n"
"Preguntas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Esto se prepara cerca de algún tipo de nueces?\"\n"
"- \"¿La salsa contiene lácteos?\"\n"
"- \"¿La sopa se hace con caldo de pollo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Esto contiene huevo crudo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Hay una versión sin gluten?\"\n"
"- \"¿Puede prepararse este plato sin queso?\"\n"
"\n"
"Para una alergia seria, no confíes solo en los símbolos impresos en el "
"menú. Explica la alergia directamente y pide al camarero que confirme con "
"la cocina.\n"
"\n"
"## Elegir Cómo Se Cocina la Carne\n"
"\n"
"Al pedir un bistec u otras carnes, el camarero puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"> \"¿Cómo le gustaría que se cocinara?\"\n"
"\n"
"Las opciones comunes incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- **Poco hecho** — cocido brevemente y rojo por dentro\n"
"- **Medio poco hecho** — tibio y rojo en el centro\n"
"- **Al punto** — rosado en el centro\n"
"- **Tres cuartos** — solo ligeramente rosado\n"
"- **Bien hecho** — completamente cocido\n"
"\n"
"Puedes responder:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Al punto, por favor.\"\n"
"- \"Lo quiero bien cocido.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría cocinarlo medio poco hecho?\"\n"
"- \"Por favor, asegúrese de que esté completamente cocido.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Confirmar Tu Pedido\n"
"\n"
"Antes de dejar la mesa, el camarero puede repetir el pedido.\n"
"\n"
"Escucha con cuidado y corrige cualquier error:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Sí, eso es correcto.\"\n"
"- \"En realidad, pedí el salmón, no el pollo.\"\n"
"- \"La ensalada debe ser sin cebolla.\"\n"
"- \"Pedimos dos sopas, no una.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría repetir los acompañamientos?\"\n"
"- \"¿Eso incluye las verduras adicionales?\"\n"
"- \"Sí, pero por favor ponga la salsa a un lado.\"\n"
"\n"
"Repetir detalles importantes ayuda a prevenir malentendidos.\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir Algo Durante la Comida\n"
"\n"
"Es posible que necesites un artículo extra después de que llegue la comida.\n"
"\n"
"Solicitudes útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos tener un poco más de agua?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría traerme otro tenedor?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos tener servilletas adicionales?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría traerme sal y pimienta?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría traernos otro plato?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener un poco de ketchup?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos obtener otra cesta de pan?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría calentarlo, por favor?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría pedir otra bebida?\"\n"
"\n"
"Para llamar la atención del camarero educadamente, di:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Disculpe.\"\n"
"- \"Perdón, ¿podría ayudarnos?\"\n"
"- \"Cuando tenga un momento, ¿podríamos tener más agua?\"\n"
"\n"
"Evita gritar o chasquear los dedos.\n"
"\n"
"## Responder Cuando el Camarero Te Pregunta\n"
"\n"
"El camarero puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Cómo está todo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Está bien su comida?\"\n"
"- \"¿Puedo traerle algo más?\"\n"
"- \"¿Está disfrutando de su comida?\"\n"
"\n"
"Si todo está bien, di:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Todo está excelente, gracias.\"\n"
"- \"La comida es deliciosa.\"\n"
"- \"Sí, todo está bien.\"\n"
"- \"Lo estamos disfrutando, gracias.\"\n"
"\n"
"Si algo está mal, esta es una buena oportunidad para explicarlo.\n"
"\n"
"## Manejar un Pedido Incorrecto\n"
"\n"
"Los errores pueden ocurrir. Explica el problema con calma y claridad.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes decir:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Disculpe, creo que este es el plato equivocado.\"\n"
"- \"Pedí el salmón, pero esto es pollo.\"\n"
"- \"Pedí esto sin queso.\"\n"
"- \"Esto no es lo que pedí.\"\n"
"- \"Todavía estamos esperando un plato.\"\n"
"- \"Creo que esto pertenece a otra mesa.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría verificar nuestro pedido, por favor?\"\n"
"\n"
"Pide una solución clara:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podría reemplazarlo, por favor?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría traer el plato que pedí?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría eliminar esto de la cuenta?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría verificar cuánto tiempo tomará el plato correcto?\"\n"
"- \"¿Sería posible mantener los otros platos calientes?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Quejarse de la Comida con Educación\n"
"\n"
"Si la comida no está bien preparada, describe el problema específico.\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"La comida está fría.\"\n"
"- \"El bistec está demasiado cocido.\"\n"
"- \"Esto es mucho más picante de lo que esperaba.\"\n"
"- \"El pollo no parece completamente cocido.\"\n"
"- \"La sopa está demasiado salada.\"\n"
"- \"Hay un ingrediente que pedí omitir.\"\n"
"- \"Este plato tiene un sabor inusual.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría pedir a la cocina que lo verifique?\"\n"
"\n"
"Una queja educada pero clara podría ser:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Disculpe, ordené el bistec al punto, pero está bien cocido. ¿Sería "
"posible reemplazarlo?\"\n"
"\n"
"No necesitas disculparte por reportar un problema genuino.\n"
"\n"
"## Preguntar sobre un Pedido Retrasado\n"
"\n"
"Si has estado esperando mucho tiempo, pregunta por una actualización:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Disculpe, ¿podría verificar nuestro pedido?\"\n"
"- \"¿Sabe cuánto tiempo más tomará?\"\n"
"- \"Llevamos esperando unos cuarenta minutos.\"\n"
"- \"¿Hay un retraso en la cocina?\"\n"
"- \"Una persona en nuestra mesa aún no ha recibido su comida.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podrían servirse todos los platos juntos?\"\n"
"- \"Necesitamos irnos pronto. ¿El pedido está casi listo?\"\n"
"\n"
"Mantén los hechos y explica lo que necesitas.\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir Postre o Café\n"
"\n"
"Después del plato principal, el camarero puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría ver el menú de postres?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le interesa un postre?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría café o té?\"\n"
"- \"¿Puedo retirar estos platos?\"\n"
"\n"
"Puedes responder:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos ver el menú de postres?\"\n"
"- \"¿Qué postres recomienda?\"\n"
"- \"Compartiremos un postre.\"\n"
"- \"Tomaré un café, por favor.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría ser un café descafeinado?\"\n"
"- \"No, gracias, sin postre.\"\n"
"- \"Solo la cuenta, por favor.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir Para Llevar las Sobras a Casa\n"
"\n"
"En algunos países y restaurantes, puedes pedir llevar contigo la comida no "
"terminada.\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podría llevar esto a casa?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría empaquetarlo para mí?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener una caja para llevar?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría empaquetar la salsa por separado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Es seguro recalentar esto mañana?\"\n"
"\n"
"También podrías escuchar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría que le empaquetara eso?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría llevar el resto con usted?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Pedir la Cuenta\n"
"\n"
"Al final de la comida, di:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos tener la cuenta, por favor?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría traerme la cuenta, por favor?\"\n"
"- \"Estamos listos para pagar.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría traer la máquina de tarjetas?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podemos pagar en la mesa?\"\n"
"- \"¿Pagamos aquí o en el mostrador?\"\n"
"\n"
"**Cuenta** es más común en inglés británico, mientras que **cheque** es más "
"común en inglés americano.\n"
"\n"
"## Pagar Juntos o Separado\n"
"\n"
"El camarero puede preguntar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Será todo junto o por separado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Le gustaría dividir la cuenta?\"\n"
"- \"¿Cómo le gustaría pagar?\"\n"
"\n"
"Respuestas útiles incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Pagaremos juntos.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos pagar por separado?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podríamos dividir la cuenta equitativamente?\"\n"
"- \"Pagaré por todo.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría pagar por estos dos artículos?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podemos usar dos tarjetas diferentes?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría dividir el total entre tres personas?\"\n"
"\n"
"Si necesitas explicar exactamente lo que ordenaste, di:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Tuve la sopa, el salmón y un agua con gas.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Verificar la Cuenta\n"
"\n"
"Antes de pagar, verifica que los artículos y el total sean correctos.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes decir:\n"
"\n"
"- \"¿Podría explicar este cargo?\"\n"
"- \"Creo que hay un artículo adicional en la cuenta.\"\n"
"- \"Solo pedimos una botella de agua.\"\n"
"- \"¿Se incluyó el cargo por servicio?\"\n"
"- \"¿La propina ya está incluida?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría eliminar este artículo? Fue devuelto.\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener una cuenta detallada?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría tener un recibo?\"\n"
"\n"
"Una **cuenta detallada** enumera cada alimento y bebida por separado.\n"
"\n"
"## Pagar y Dejar Propina\n"
"\n"
"Frases útiles al pagar incluyen:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Pagaré con tarjeta.\"\n"
"- \"¿Puedo pagar en efectivo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Aceptan pagos sin contacto?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría pagar en una moneda diferente?\"\n"
"- \"¿Podría darme un recibo?\"\n"
"- \"¿Puedo agregar una propina con tarjeta?\"\n"
"- \"¿Está incluido el servicio?\"\n"
"- \"Por favor, quédese con el cambio.\"\n"
"\n"
"Las costumbres de propina varían según el país. Verifica si ya se ha "
"agregado un cargo por servicio antes de dejar una propina adicional.\n"
"\n"
"## Una Conversación Sencilla en un Restaurante\n"
"\n"
"Una conversación típica podría verse así:\n"
"\n"
"> **Camarero:** Buenas noches. ¿Tiene una reserva?  \n"
"> **Cliente:** Sí, reservé una mesa para dos a nombre de Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Camarero:** Por supuesto. Por favor, sígame. ¿Le traigo algo de beber?  "
"\n"
"> **Cliente:** ¿Podríamos tener una botella de agua sin gas, por favor?  \n"
"> **Camarero:** Claro. ¿Está listo para ordenar?  \n"
"> **Cliente:** Necesito otro minuto. ¿Qué recomendaría para alguien que le "
"gusta el pescado?  \n"
"> **Camarero:** El salmón a la parrilla es muy popular. Viene con papas y "
"verduras.  \n"
"> **Cliente:** ¿La salsa contiene lácteos?  \n"
"> **Camarero:** Sí, pero podemos servirlo sin la salsa.  \n"
"> **Cliente:** Estupendo. Tomaré el salmón sin salsa. ¿Podría cambiar las "
"papas por una ensalada?  \n"
"> **Camarero:** Por supuesto.  \n"
"> **Cliente:** Gracias.\n"
"\n"
"## Una Fórmula Sencilla para el Restaurante\n"
"\n"
"Usa esta estructura durante una visita al restaurante:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Llegar:** Confirma tu reserva o pide una mesa.\n"
"2. **Preguntar:** Solicita el menú y pregunta sobre los platos "
"desconocidos.\n"
"3. **Elegir:** Ordena comida y bebida claramente.\n"
"4. **Aclarar:** Explica las alergias, preferencias y cambios solicitados.\n"
"5. **Confirmar:** Escucha mientras el camarero repite el pedido.\n"
"6. **Responder:** Pide cualquier otra cosa que necesites durante la comida.\n"
"7. **Resolver:** Explica cualquier problema y solicita una solución.\n"
"8. **Pagar:** Pide la cuenta, revísala y elige un método de pago.\n"
"\n"
"Por ejemplo:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Me gustaría el pollo a la parrilla, pero ¿podría tenerlo sin cebolla y "
"con una ensalada en lugar de papas fritas?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Escenario de Práctica\n"
"\n"
"En esta representación, estás cenando en el Riverside Kitchen. El camarero "
"de IA te dará la bienvenida, te ayudará a entender el menú, tomará tu orden "
"y responderá a tus solicitudes.\n"
"\n"
"Durante la conversación, intenta:\n"
"\n"
"- Pedir una mesa o confirmar una reserva.\n"
"- Pedir una bebida y un plato principal.\n"
"- Hacer al menos una pregunta sobre un elemento del menú.\n"
"- Solicitar una recomendación.\n"
"- Mencionar una preferencia dietética o pedir un cambio.\n"
"- Confirmar un detalle importante sobre tu pedido.\n"
"- Responder a un pequeño problema con la comida o el servicio.\n"
"- Pedir la cuenta y explicar cómo te gustaría pagar.\n"
"\n"
"Concéntrate en comunicar claramente y con educación. La gramática perfecta "
"es menos importante que asegurarte de que el camarero entienda tu pedido y "
"tus necesidades."

